A '''Veteran''' (Japanese: '''ベテラントレーナー''' ''Veteran Trainer'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in the [[Generation IV]] games. In Generation IV, they are depicted as healthy old men in old-fashioned clothing, a white {{wp|keikogi}} and a red {{wp|hakama}}. In {{game|Black and White|s}}, Veterans are depicted as much younger people in trenchcoats; they seem to be adult versions of {{tc|Ace Trainer}}s. Also, female Veterans were introduced. Some will give out [[PP Max]]es after they are defeated.

They are similar to the {{tc|Expert}} Trainer class of [[Generation III]], but use a variety of high-leveled, usually fully evolved Pokémon similar to Ace Trainers. In the [[Battle Subway]], [[Battle Maison]], and [[Battle Tree]], they tend to specialize in [[Legendary Pokémon]].

A male Veteran can team up with a male Ace Trainer or a female Veteran to form a duo known as {{tc|Master & Apprentice}} or {{tc|Veteran Duo}}, respectively, and challenge the {{player}} to a [[Double Battle]].

In [[Generation VII]], Veterans keep their Pokémon in [[Ultra Ball]]s. Some of them also possess [[Z-Ring]]s{{sup/7|SM}} or [[Z-Power Ring]]s{{sup/7|USUM}}.

